> 
> I don't think this would work...?  If it did, the logical extension
> would be that you could get rid of any loadstone easily by putting it
> in a container and dropping the container.

It does, though. 

The loadstone is intrinsically heavy, it doesn't magically become heavy
the moment you pick it up. 

You can pick up a loadstone in a box (or a bag) without any trouble,
except that it's heavy, but if you have a "bare" loadstone in your
inventory it can't leave your person while it's cursed, meaning you
can't drop it, put it in a box or bag, throw it, or shoot it with a
sling.

So if you pick up a box only containing one gray stone, and it makes you
Stressed instead of plain Burdened, it's pretty certain that the stone
is a loadstone. Unfortunately, the only way to #name it is to take it
out, meaning that naming it is only feasible if you can cast remove
curse, have remove curse scrolls to spare, or were going to read a
scroll of remove curse to uncurse other things anyway.

